Hint:\( v(t) = \frac{dx}{dt}\)

Step: Find the velocity of the particle.The velocity \(v(t)\) is the first derivative of the position function is given
by;
\(\Rightarrow v(t) = \frac{dx}{dt}\)
Differentiating \(x(t) = 2t^2\)we get;
\(\Rightarrow v(t) = \frac{d}{dt}(2t^2) = 4t\)
Now, substitute \(t=2\) seconds into the velocity equation we get;
\(\Rightarrow v(2) = 4 \times 2 = 8 \, \text{m/s}\)
